Don't: 
    Expect AI to solve everything
Do: 
    Be realistic about what AI can and cannot do given limitations of technology, data, and     engineering resources

Don't: 
    Hire 2-3 ML engineers and count soley on them to come up with use cases
Do: 
    Pair engineering talent with business talet and work cross-functionally to find             feasible and valuable projects. 

Don't:
    Expect the AI project to work the first time
Do: 
    Plan for AI development to be an iteratice process with multiple attempts needed to succeed. 

Don't: 
    Expect traditional planning processes to apply without changes
Do: 
    Work with AI team to establish timeline estimates, milestones, KPIs, etc. 

Don't:
    Think you need superstar AI engineers before you do anything 
Do:
    Keep bulding and working with the team you have and grow with them
